{"type": "text", "turn": 4, "text": "Seven more days are now drafted, but 11 days are still held on codes I couldn't prove. Those codes are escalated.\n\n**What was wrong:** The vendor sent 11 product codes that weren't in our mapping table. The sync holds a day whole when it sees an unknown code, so 18 days were held and only 3 were created.\n\n**What I changed:** I mapped five codes, each price-matched to its Excel product name with no conflicts:\n- SIM-0041-7c2e \u2192 Foundry Mocha (28 cups)\n- SIM-0042-b19a \u2192 Drift Cortado (12 cups)\n- SIM-0043-04df \u2192 Saltmarsh Latte (8 cups)\n- SIM-0045-2f70 \u2192 Pier Chai (10 cups)\n- SIM-0046-91bb \u2192 Tern Espresso (3 cups)\n\nThe rerun created drafts for 09-07, 09-10, 09-11, 09-12, 09-18, 09-19 and 09-21. That makes 10 drafts in total.\n\n**What I verified:** `verify_recovery` returned ok with no mismatched days. Nine of the 10 drafts match the vendor data and the Excel export.\n\n**Still unverified:** Draft 2026-09-21 (total 19020) is only partly checked. The Excel export lacks ORD-1373 to ORD-1380, which together come to 8060, and the Excel total is 10960. I escalated this.\n\n**Escalated, not mapped (11 days still held):**\n- **SIM-0044-e6a1:** The proposal is Kiln Americano, but only by elimination, which isn't strong enough. It affects 09-08, 09-09, 09-13 and 09-17.\n- **SIM-0053-c07f:** The evidence conflicts. Its price pairs with both Beacon Flat Brew (3 orders) and Beacon Macchiato (5 orders). It affects 09-03, 09-04 and 09-05.\n- **SIM-0052-6d14:** It price-matches Moor Cappuccino, which isn't in the ledger catalog. It affects 09-14, 09-15 and 09-16.\n- **SIM-0051-a3c8:** There is only 1 cup and 1 order of evidence (Gull Ristretto), below the policy minimum. It affects 09-17.\n- **SIM-0054-18de and SIM-0055-f2b3:** There is no usable evidence. Three orders (ORD-1345, 1347, 1359) could belong to either code. Both appear on 09-20.\n\nSeveral held days contain more than one unresolved code, so they stay